# =============================================================================
# .vercelignore — Monorepo root
# =============================================================================
# Vercel reads this file from the repo root to decide which files are synced
# to the build container (across ALL Vercel projects from this repo).
#
# WHY root-level placement matters:
# - Vercel syncs the ENTIRE repo to the build container first, then applies
#   Root Directory filter. Without .vercelignore, huge folders like
#   server/, node_modules, dist/, .obsidian/ would be uploaded — wasting
#   sync time and potentially hitting Vercel's 100 MB source limit.
# - A root-level file covers both UserUI and DashboardUI Vercel projects.
# - Subfolder .vercelignore files are NOT read by Vercel; only root matters.
# =============================================================================

# ----- Dependencies (huge; always reinstalled by Vercel's npm install) -----
node_modules/

# ----- Build output (rebuilt by Vercel; local dist/ is stale) -----
dist/

# ----- Server backend (NOT part of frontend deploy; very large) -----
server/

# ----- Environment / secrets (never deploy) -----
.env
.env.*

# ----- Editor / IDE config -----
.obsidian/
.opencode/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ----- Documentation / non-code -----
memory/
*.md

# ----- OS artifacts -----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ----- Test / coverage -----
coverage/
*.log
